Subject: [PATCH] dwc2: skip clear_force_mode debounce on role-switch platforms
Upstream-Status: Pending

Split out of the old
0022-dwc2-remove-3x100ms-overhead-when-booting-with-USB_DR_MODE_OTG-and-Ingenic-X1600.patch,
which mixed this behavioural change with unrelated logging and with an
unrelated params.c change (now
0044-dwc2-use-fixed-FIFO-parameters-on-the-Ingenic-X1600-family.patch) under
a subject that described none of them.

dwc2_clear_force_mode() drops the GUSBCFG force bits and then sleeps 100ms
to wait out the IDDIG debounce filter, because the core falls back to
whatever the ID pin reports. On a platform that drives the role from a
usb_role_switch with dr_mode=OTG, nothing consumes that fallback state -
the next mode change calls dwc2_force_mode() again, which waits on its own.
The sleep only costs probe time and adds latency to every role switch.

Note this is about dwc2_clear_force_mode() only. The debounce in
dwc2_core_reset() is a different matter: there the core genuinely needs the
time, and the ~100ms is observable on hardware.

Also drops a commented-out dwc2_is_ingenic_x1600_family() call that the old
patch left behind at this site - the helper is static to params.c and was
never callable from here.

---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/core.c |  12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core.c
@@ -616,6 +616,18 @@
 	gusbcfg &= ~GUSBCFG_FORCEDEVMODE;
 	dwc2_writel(hsotg, gusbcfg, GUSBCFG);
 
+	/*
+	 * The msleep() below exists to wait out the IDDIG debounce filter after
+	 * the force bits are dropped and the core falls back to whatever the ID
+	 * pin says. On a usb-role-switch platform with dr_mode=OTG there is no
+	 * consumer for that fallback state: every mode change goes through
+	 * dwc2_force_mode() again, which does its own waiting. Paying 100ms
+	 * here only delays probe and every subsequent role switch.
+	 */
+	if (hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG &&
+	    device_property_read_bool(hsotg->dev, "usb-role-switch"))
+		return;
+
 	if (dwc2_iddig_filter_enabled(hsotg))
 		msleep(100);
 }
